---
description: Compose the actual vault goal from retained evidence and exact native effects.
args:
  goal: string
returns: OpenVaultReport
---
Resolve the user's actual vault question or authorized edit using the current editor and relevant retained evidence. Decide which navigation, review or revision is needed next; the pure decision child can help interpret the current view and observation history, while the native change helper applies an exact proposed change and returns its real result and fresh readback. Retain the views and actual operation feedback, including unavailable navigation and rejected revisions, rather than treating an attempted operation as success.

Use exact observed link identities, current revisions and authorized source scope. Preserve unrelated source and concurrent edits. Reconsider new evidence when returning to a note or after a changed revision; an earlier successful edit need not be repeated. Choose review checks for the actual request, keeping literal requested values and real render/committed-source evidence distinct. Return the typed review of the relevant current document, or explain a real blocker. Do not invent a publication, commit or external delivery capability.
